# User compiles (do not run builds yourself)

The user compiles and builds locally. **Do not** run compile or build commands unless they explicitly ask you to in that conversation.

## Do not run (unless asked)

- WASM: `compil2Wasm.sh`, `emcmake`, Emscripten builds in `sker/`
- App sync: `npm run build`, copying WASM artifacts to `skeepto/build/`
- Native C++ builds in `sker/` (CMake, make, xcodebuild, etc.)

## Instead

After C++/WASM or frontend changes that require a rebuild, **tell the user** what to run — do not launch it yourself.

Example reminder (WASM + skeepto):

```bash
cd /Users/stephaneallez/Projects/skeepto-engine
cmake -B build-wasm -DSK_PLATFORM=wasm -DSK_SKEEPTO_DIR=/Users/stephaneallez/Projects/skeepto
cmake --build build-wasm --parallel
cd /Users/stephaneallez/Projects/skeepto && npm run build
```

Then hard-refresh (**Cmd+Shift+R**) when testing `.wasm` changes.

## When you may compile

Only when the user explicitly asks, e.g. “compile le WASM”, “lance npm run build”, “build et teste”.
